      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given unpredictable lead times from Shenzhen, you should base your safety stock on variability rather than just average demand. A good starting point is calculating safety stock as: $\\text{Z-score} \\times \\text{Standard Deviation of Demand during Lead Time}$. Use a higher Z-score (like 1.645 for 95% service level) if avoiding stockouts is critical. Tracking historical order and delivery times will help you accurately calculate that standard deviation.",
