    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i get that, but the \"unseen\" part is what's frustrating. like, there aren't really any social media trends for specific battery cells, and our suppliers are pretty responsive. it literally feels like things just... vanish or get messed up for no reason. is there any way to factor in those types of random, almost \"mischievous\" errors into the logic? like if the data itself is being compromised by something we can't track?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the issues feel random and untraceable, the problem might be process-related rather than purely statistical. Implementing a rigorous, multi-point physical inventory audit process can help catch discrepancies between system records and actual stock. Additionally, segment your inventory into tiers: perhaps the most critical components get a fixed, high safety stock buffer regardless of minor statistical fluctuations. This acts as a manual safeguard against unexplainable data loss or administrative errors.",
      "source": "target",
